Evaluation

Without a purchased license, you may install official evaluation builds for
personal evaluation, testing, and feedback. Evaluation access does not grant a
license for paid client work or other production business use.

Purchased license

A completed, non-refunded purchase grants the named purchaser a non-exclusive
license to use the purchased major version for personal and commercial work,
including client deliverables, on computers that purchaser owns or controls.
Each additional user needs a separate license. Keep your receipt as proof of
purchase. A support payment alone does not purchase this license.

For new managed-license purchases, checkout identifies either a one-time license
for the purchased major version or a subscription. A one-time license does not
require a recurring purchase; maintenance updates for its purchased major version
are included. A subscription permits the features and versions identified by its
plan while access remains active. Future major versions for a one-time license
are separate purchases unless the order expressly includes them.

Managed access requires license-key activation and periodic online verification.
The default limit is two active installations and up to seven days of verified
offline access; the applicable limits and renewal terms must be shown before
checkout. When verified access expires, new edits and new assistant operations
are unavailable, while viewing, saving, and exporting existing work remain
available. Refunds, revoked installations, and disabled licenses can remove
editing access on the next verification; an already issued offline lease remains
bounded by its signed expiry. Subscription cancellation retains access through
the provider's verified paid-through date unless the purchase is refunded or
otherwise disabled. No customer documents are deleted because access ends.

Previously granted receipt-only licenses retain their original rights, including
use of the purchased major version without a subscription or periodic activation.
They are not silently converted to managed licenses or subscriptions. This does
not promise future features, a particular update schedule, or indefinite support
for operating systems or hardware.

